<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Ball and Chain</h1>
<p>Average Length: Approx. varied
Type of Weapon: Distanced Hand-to-hand.
</p><p>Ball and chain was the common name for the ball and chain mace. It consisted of a heavy metal ball, often spiked, attached to a wooden handle by means of a chain. A form of flail weapon and essentially a version of the morning star is appearance and use, the ball and chain was extremely effective at getting around an opponent’s shield, yanking the shield away, pulling a rider off a mount, or simply smashing armor. The ball and chain uses the momentum of the swing to create greater force upon impact with the target.
</p><p>The center of gravity of the ball and chain weapon is in the ball itself. Thus, by winding up a swing before striking, the wielder could sometimes double, even triple the force of impact with the target. Needless to say, this weapon was very effective at creating crushing and stunning blows, even against an armored opponent. Further, if the ball was spiked, the force of the blow concentrated at the tip of the spike was devastatingly effective at piercing through armor.
</p>
<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="In_Valhalla">In Valhalla</span></h2>
<p>In Valhalla the ball and chain is fought with the flail skill, one of the clubs and maces (see <a cmd='#'>Help Weapons</a>): two-handed, it bludgeons, it leans on strength, with some dexterity, and it is slow, as two-handed weapons are. It is taught by the barbarians from guild level 14, the fighters from guild level 14, the necromancers from guild level 14 (up to 70%), the knights from guild level 15, the paladins from guild level 15 and the healers from guild level 34 (up to 70%).
</p><p><br />
